### Why this fixes the lobby case
In the pre-join lobby `MeetView` has `currentMeet === null`, so `publishLocalMedia()` never writes a stream to `activeMeets` — that's why the old `cameraOn` (which read only the store stream) returned `false`. Now `startLocalCamera()` sets the global `localCameraEnabled` flag directly, `Tab.vue` reads it, and the cam icon appears as soon as the camera turns on — in the lobby and during a call alike. Turning the camera off (toggle, settings, leave, end, or unmount) clears the flag and hides the icon.

